    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW27uhpWJtUHF98AG4RpLvEcX)_\n\n## Merge order\n- Base: `main`, which already contains #453 (merged) and #462.\n- Touches only `sp-pdf-reader` (`.el` and its literate `.org`).\n- Independent of every open PR; nothing breaks in either merge order.\n\n## What\n- Cause of \"emureader does not load\" and `elpaca-update-all` failing with `(wrong-type-argument stringp nil)` in `elpaca-git--fetch`:\n  - Elpaca's cached GNU ELPA menu (`var/elpaca/cache/gnu-elpa.eld`) was last written on Oct 7.\n  - emureader was renamed from emacs-reader on Nov 4 (0.4.0), so the cached menu has no recipe for it.\n  - `:ensure t` then queues a recipe with no repository; the fetch fails, nothing is built, and `apropos` finds no `emureader-*` command.\n  - `lsp-mode` fails only because it waits on emureader.\n- Fix: `use-package emureader :ensure (:repo \"https://codeberg.org/MonadicSheep/emureader.git\")` (the upstream GNU ELPA mirrors).\n- Literate doc updated as bullet lists (reason, build step, what is still unverified).\n\n## Not verified\n- `emureader-build` exists (0.4.0 NEWS on elpa.gnu.org).\n- `emureader-open-doc` and `emureader-goto-page` are still assumed; the source could not be fetched from the cloud container.\n- `litdb` failing in the same run looks unrelated (its checkout is a normal clone of `jkitchin/litdb`); the Elpaca log is needed.\n\n## Manual testing\n- [ ] `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 463-emureader-recipe; git checkout 463-emureader-recipe`, restart Emacs.\n- [ ] `M-x elpaca-update-all` no longer reports an error for emureader, and `lsp-mode` builds.\n- [ ] `~/.config/emacs-modular/var/elpaca/sources/emureader` exists.\n- [ ] `brew install mupdf gcc make`, then `M-x emureader-build` works.\n- [ ] `M-: (progn (require 'emureader) (list (fboundp 'emureader-open-doc) (fboundp 'emureader-goto-page)))` → `(t t)`; if not, `M-x apropos RET emureader-.*\\(open\\|page\\)` and set the `sp-pdf-reader-function-*` variables.\n- [ ] `M-x sp-pdf-open` on a PDF opens it in emureader; `C-u` and page 5 opens at page 5.\n- [ ] Embark `p` on a DEVONthink record opens the PDF in emureader.\n- [ ] If Elpaca still fails: send the `*elpaca-log*` lines for emureader and litdb.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCdC2Z3W8k8foAG8mF)_",
